This was the end of my promising barbarian Bjoern, on Yeenoghu's level 
(whom he had killed with one salvo of five +4 bullets and who had not 
even got the chance to teleport to the upstairs).

Bjoern went downstairs with three of his pets, just to see he had 
arrived at the top level of the wizard's tower.  He went upstairs again 
to whistle close his last pet, the planetar.  Then he got a message 
which I found again in a file called "paniclog" in the slashem 
directory: "trickery Cannot create file "Klaus Kassner-bjoern.0" for 
level 0 (errno 13)", followed by "DYWYPI?".  Sigh.  I knew that slash'em 
is less stable than NH, but I had hoped that no game crash would prevent 
an ascension this time (one of my three explore mode games had ended 
similarly - the guy was also on a staircase, but it happened when I 
restarted the game, this time it was fully in game).

I guess I might as well wait until a more stable version of the game is 
available :-(.  (Does this happen on Linux computers, too, or is this 
specific for Windows? I might install the game on a Linux PC if it runs 
more stably there.)  Well, at least the game will not disturb my 
Christmas now...

